; V3DDriver.cmhg - CMHG module header for the M0/M1 V3D driver sketch.
;
; SWI chunk number, per ROOL documented allocation rules
; (see riscosopen.org/content/allocate and the Introduction To SWIs
; wiki page for the bit layout):
;   bits 18-19 of the SWI number select the SWI group - 00=OS,
;   01=OS modules, 10=third-party (officially allocated), 11=user
;   applications (free for private/development use, it is the
;   author responsibility to avoid clashes on their own machine).
; 0xC0040 = group 0b11 (user applications, bits 18-19) plus chunk
; number 1 (bits 6-16). This replaces an earlier placeholder (0x50EC0)
; that sat in the OS modules group by mistake - safe for private dev
; use, but NOT for release: before this is shared with anyone else,
; request a real allocation via !Allocate to allocate@riscosopen.org.

title-string:            V3DDriver
help-string:              V3DDriver 0.01 (M0/M1 sketch, not for release)
initialisation-code:      module_init
finalisation-code:        module_final
swi-chunk-base-number:    0xC0040
swi-handler-code:         v3d_swi_handler
swi-decoding-table:       V3D,PowerOn,ReadIdent
